Installation:

1. run setup.py
   python setup.py install 

2. create shared object library
   cd robocop
   ./gccCompile

3. update shared object library path config.ini
   cshared=<your new path>/librobocop.so

Running:

1. To run using EM
   robocop.py <coordinate file -- e.g. analysis/coordinates.bed> <config file -- e.g. analysis/config.ini> <output directory>

2. To run without EM
   robocop_no_em.py <coordinate file -- e.g. unit_test/coordinates.bed> <config file -- e.g. analysis/config.ini> <output directory> <output directory generated by robocop.py> <output directory>


---- permol_seq_maskoff_logfull_nucbrogsym (2026-10-28) ----
Copy of pkgvar/permol_seq_maskoff_logfull. Only change: robocop/robocop.py reads the nucleosome
m6A profile from inputs/nucleosome_params_brogaard_sym.pkl (NUC_PARAMS_FILE) instead of
inputs/nucleosome_params.pkl, in the aggregate path and in build_fiber_ps (which gains an
optional nuc_file argument). Built by analysis/nucbrogsym/ (see m6a_fit.py).

---- permol_seq_maskoff_logfull_nucbrogsym_all7 (2026-10-30) ----
Copy of pkgvar/permol_seq_maskoff_logfull_nucbrogsym. Only change: robocop/robocop.py reads
inputs/nucleosome_params_brogaard_sym_all7.pkl (NUC_PARAMS_FILE) and inputs/bg_params_all7.pkl
(BG_PARAMS_FILE, new) instead of the barcode01 files, in the aggregate path and in build_fiber_ps
(which gains an optional bg_file argument). Both refitted on the merged 7-barcode pileup by
analysis/nucbrogsym/bg_fit.py and m6a_fit.py --pileup. TF params unchanged.

---- permol_seq_maskoff_logfull_nucbrogsym_filt (2026-11-02) ----
Copy of pkgvar/permol_seq_maskoff_logfull_nucbrogsym_all7. Only change: robocop/robocop.py reads
inputs/nucleosome_params_brogaard_sym_filt.pkl (NUC_PARAMS_FILE), inputs/bg_params_filt.pkl
(BG_PARAMS_FILE) and inputs/all_TFs_1000pealVal_params_pseudo_filt.pkl (new TF_PARAMS_FILE constant,
used in the aggregate path and in build_fiber_ps, which gains an optional tf_file argument).
All three are fitted on the filtered 7-barcode pileup (/usr/project/xtmp/nd141/filtered_refit/):
primary, MAPQ>=20, aligned length>=500, qs>=10, pooled median+-4*1.4826*MAD per-read m6A cap,
fixed modkit threshold. Fits: nucbrogsym/bg_fit.py, nucbrogsym/m6a_fit.py, nucbrogsym/tf_fit.py.
